            <ArticleTitle>Questions from and answers to a patient with groin hernia.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0003469X17027336</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Inguinal hernia surgical treatment are the most commonly performed operations in general surgery practice. There is a need for detailed anatomical knowledge and surgical skills to satisfactorily treat this disease. In this review, we aimed to present up-to-date information and approaches on basic diagnosis, treatment, complications and management of inguinal hernias in our institution.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="KEY WORDS" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">Chronic pain, Groin hernia, Inguinal hernia, Recurrence, Surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
